1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,175
You ask an AI to subscribe you to
software.

2
00:00:03,175 --> 00:00:05,291
It gets “under 200 a month.”

3
00:00:05,291 --> 00:00:08,465
But will it hit pay when you’re not
watching?

4
00:00:08,465 --> 00:00:11,993
Most agents never spend — or spend with no
explanation.

5
00:00:11,993 --> 00:00:15,167
MandatePay: the AI can judge on its own —

6
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:19,400
but every judgment is explainable, and
every payment gets a human nod.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,047
First, authorize it. One sentence:

8
00:00:31,247 --> 00:00:36,121
And this isn’t keyword matching. It’s
function calling

9
00:00:36,121 --> 00:00:40,995
The model picks the tool and the
arguments.

10
00:00:40,995 --> 00:00:44,651
It pulled out a monthly budget

11
00:00:44,651 --> 00:00:50,744
A per-transaction limit, a vendor list,
and a category list.

12
00:00:50,744 --> 00:00:53,791
That’s an executable Intent Mandate.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,384
Now give it something a human would
actually say:

14
00:01:04,684 --> 00:01:10,043
A rule parser dies here. It can pull out
the numbers

15
00:01:10,043 --> 00:01:13,940
But “the cheaper one” needs both prices
first.

16
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:16,376
Look at the tool trace

17
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:22,221
It queried Notion, then Figma, and only
then created the purchase request.

18
00:01:22,221 --> 00:01:28,554
It found Notion at ten a month, Figma at
fifteen — and decided.

19
00:01:28,554 --> 00:01:33,913
That’s reasoning, not classification.
Query, compare, decide — on its own.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,083
Now it hits the allowlist. The verdict is
REJECT. And notice

21
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:42,394
It doesn’t just say “denied”.

22
00:01:46,294 --> 00:01:50,915
First, the insight: here’s where your
wallet stands this month.

23
00:01:50,915 --> 00:01:58,771
Second, the explanation: not a cold no —
which rule blocked it, and how to fix it.

24
00:01:58,771 --> 00:02:03,392
That fix isn’t a template — the model
generated it

25
00:02:03,392 --> 00:02:08,938
Add Slack to the allowlist and it can
charge the company card.

26
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,420
But if it decides this is worth buying, it
still can’t charge you.

27
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:21,853
Over the threshold, so it stops — the
status is PAYER_ACTION_REQUIRED.

28
00:02:21,853 --> 00:02:24,816
Every request carries a
three-layer Mandate

29
00:02:24,816 --> 00:02:26,298
Intent, Cart, Payment.

30
00:02:31,498 --> 00:02:33,473
Human authorizes, machine executes.

31
00:02:33,473 --> 00:02:38,906
And here it is in PayPal — order
<ORDER_ID>, status COMPLETED.

32
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,048
Everything is auditable — used, remaining,
and month-end projection, all computed.

33
00:02:44,048 --> 00:02:47,360
Every trace_id shows the
Intent, Cart and Payment layers

34
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,464
AUTO_APPROVE, REQUIRE_HUMAN, REJECT.

35
00:02:48,464 --> 00:02:50,304
Six hundred and fifty decisions

36
00:02:50,304 --> 00:02:53,616
Three independent implementations. Four
wrong-verdict classes — all fixed.

37
00:02:53,616 --> 00:02:58,032
MandatePay — let AI spend, but every cent
earns your authorization. Thanks.
